From 3ea3e88ece6af6c65cf967020fcfb9b41f44d968 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 05:49:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Name a pinned machine's core-update drain in create,
 queue and chat-wait notes

t_01a1cca8ed755919: a MacBook card pinned to hub at 21:49:38 UTC (11-11) landed inside the
hub's core-update drain (claims stopped 21:48:56, drain hold 21:50:01, claims resumed 22:14:20).
The create reply said it runs on hub and kanban_show said 'queued, not stuck', so the chat
archived it at 22:08 as lost. The body's local marker was not the cause (pickup test included).

The origin now reads the target machine's Board registry drain_active/drain_until_ms metrics
(ignored when the sample is older than 15 min): the create note, kanban_show queue note and the
chat-wait notice say DRAINING with the announced bound instead of promising a start.
